      <revisionDesc>
          <change when="2015-02-13T12:09:53.638-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/james.cowey">Finalized - Ready. I would also like to observe that on the very good image of the papyrus from Berkeley the initial Tau of the name Ταφορ is not as clear as it might be. I am unable to suggest a more convincing reading.</change>
          <change when="2015-02-13T12:09:53.632-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/james.cowey">Vote - AcceptText - There are other possibilities. Ταφορσόις is attested. When one considers that there are also attestations for Τεφορσῶς and Τεφορᾶς which are variants of the same name, it is clear that what is suggested is not exhaustive. I suggest leaving the proposed alternative reading. This note should make clear that other solutions are also quite imaginable. See also www.trismegistos/nam/detail.php?record=1433.</change>
          <change when="2015-02-13T12:09:53.625-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/berkes.lajos">Vote - AcceptText - accept, but &lt;:&lt;:(Ταφορ(σάιτος))|alt|(Ταφορ(σάειτος)):&gt;=PN N. Reggiani|ed|&lt;:(|Ταφορ|):&gt;:&gt;</change>
          <change when="2012-03-21T07:15:23.568-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/nicola.reggiani">line 6: (|Ταφορ|) -&gt; &lt;:(Ταφορ(σάιτος))|alt|(Ταφορ(σάειτος)):&gt; (cf. SB I 5124, passim, &amp; SB XIV 11355, 4).</change>
